    },
    {
     "repo": "gov",
     "path": "tools/run-gates/profile_bar.py",
     "symbol": "check_quiet",
     "binding": "SHOULD",
     "need": "command line per process (Windows namespace), liveness assertion, bounded query cost",
     "how": "This is the only reader of real argv on Windows: a `Get-CimInstance Win32_Process` query through powershell. Reuse its liveness rule, under which the query must return THIS pid's row with a non-empty CommandLine or the result is 'unverified'. Reuse its cost lesson too: an unfiltered CIM enumeration dominated the runtime, so it was filtered. Extend the query with ParentProcessId, CreationDate and KernelModeTime/UserModeTime for the Windows parent graph, age and CPU. Keep the injected `_runner` seam.",
     "half": "code"
    },
    {
     "repo": "gov",
     "path": "tools/run-gates/run-gates.sh",
     "symbol": "ts_alive / ts_sweep_queue (pid reach note)",
     "binding": "SHOULD",
     "need": "namespace question answered in the data",
     "how": "The turnstile already records that two msys runtimes need not share a pid table. Because of that, `kill -0` on a recorded pid is used only as a NEGATIVE signal that withholds a sweep, never one that grants it. The new view should carry the namespace (msys pid vs winpid, and which runtime) on each row, so consumers like ts_alive stop having to reason it out locally. Migrate ts_alive onto it, or leave it alone and document why.",
     "half": "code"
    },
    {
     "repo": "gov",
     "path": "tools/run-gates/run-selftests.sh",
     "symbol": "sweep worker pid recording + wall watchdog",
     "binding": "SHOULD",
     "need": "identity correctness (which pid is the worker)",
     "how": "This is a second consumer and an identity trap to encode in the view's contract. `$$` in a subshell is the RUNNER's pid, so the code records `$!` of the `timeout` child, and the watchdog then kills by those recorded pids. A shared view would let the watchdog confirm a recorded pid is still the same process (pid plus start time) before signalling it.",
     "half": "code"
